  "readmeFile": "README.NuGet.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.14.0. New: saved connections. devop-dk login --connection NAME stores a verified token (hidden prompt) as a named connection in its own user-only token file, with the company name; connection list (--json), connection show [NAME], connection set default NAME, connection rename OLD NEW, connection remove NAME --yes, and logout --connection NAME manage them, and never show a token. The global --connection NAME option (before or after any command) and DKPLUS_CONNECTION choose one; precedence is --connection, DKPLUS_API_TOKEN, DKPLUS_API_TOKEN_FILE, DKPLUS_CONNECTION, the stored default, then the single login, and a --connection connection keeps its own base URL and language over DKPLUS_BASE_URL and DKPLUS_ACCEPT_LANGUAGE (with a warning). connection show without a name shows what the next command uses, with each value's source. An unknown name exits with 1 and never falls back, a value containing a GUID is refused as a name and masked in messages, and an environment token that overrides DKPLUS_CONNECTION or the stored default warns on stderr. Connection metadata is kept in connections/connections.json in a user-only folder, never in config.json. config set baseUrl, language, or salesPerson with --connection sets that connection's own value. A command that changes remote state writes Using connection 'NAME' (COMPANY). on stderr when the connection is not the default login. login and logout without --connection keep using the single token file, so earlier versions keep working; update the CLI and the module together, since 0.13 and earlier ignore the stored default and DKPLUS_CONNECTION. Changes of the saved connections hold a lock file; a corrupt connections.json fails only commands that need a saved connection. Improvements: a verified login also reads the company name (one more read-only request; its failure never fails the login). Fixes: none.",
